  "author_association": "MEMBER",
  "body": "Every fzt-picker release's hook DLL stays loaded in a program after its injector exits, and each copy patched `CoCreateInstance` on top of the last, so when one unloaded the program crashed in freed code (at Terminal did as home-sync restarted fzt-picker). Now only the copy holding a per-process named mutex patches; another takes over from `HookProc` once it unloads. Tested by loading two copies from two paths into one process and unloading them in turn: the current release crashes with `0xC0000005`, this build keeps `CoCreateInstance` working throughout.\n\nhttps://openproject.romaine.life/wp/FZT-61",
